id: 308
data: {"t":"d","text":"The cost of a wedding lehenga can vary widely depending on factors like the designer, fabric, embroidery, and where you're sourcing it from. Here's a general guideline:\n\n1. **Budget Range**:  \n   - **Local Boutiques**: $200–$800 (₹15,000–₹60,000)  \n   - Great for simpler designs or lighter embroidery. Perfect for smaller or intimate weddings.\n\n2. **Mid-Range**:  \n   - **Established Designers or High-End Stores**: $800–$3,000 (₹60,000–₹2,50,000)  \n   - You’ll find exquisite handwork, premium fabrics, and trend-forward designs in this range. Ideal for grand weddings.\n\n3. **Luxury Range**:  \n   - **Top Designers** (e.g., Sabyasachi, Manish Malhotra): $3,000–$10,000+ (₹2,50,000–₹10,00,000+)  \n   - Lavish fabrics, intricate detailing, and custom options. This is the dream-come-true range for many brides.\n\n4. **Custom-Made Lehengas**: Costs depend on the level of customization, but starting prices can be comparable to mid-range options, going up significantly with intricate work.  \n\nShipping costs and duties (if importing) can also add to your budget, so plan accordingly. \n\nAre you leaning towards a particular budget or style? I’d love to help refine your search!","toolActions":[],"mode":"stylist","detectedLanguage":"en","responseLanguage":"en","audioUrl":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageUrls":[],"products":[],"productsHasMore":false}

